# `TopicParam`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`TopicParam` converts a value used in a typed topic destination into its wire-safe path segment. Implement it for a domain identifier only when that identifier has one stable textual representation suitable for routing. Keep encoding and validation with the identifier type so publishers and subscribers cannot disagree about a destination.

## Implementors

The generated protocol codecs can use every type listed below as a topic parameter. Prefer an existing implementor for scalar identifiers; introduce a wrapper type when an identifier needs escaping, normalization, or validation before it becomes part of a destination.

<SymbolImpls />
